{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon","id":1362697,"title":"TC: Aeon Ready-Made Characters (Trinity Continuum: Aeon)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-22T12:00:20-08:00","id":1362697,"title":"TC: Aeon Ready-Made Characters (Trinity Continuum: Aeon)","content":"The 1/20 meeting notes list this product I purchased from Drivethrurpg as being in post editing development. Huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T20:56:34-08:00","id":1362791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon#post1362697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 1/20 meeting notes list this product I purchased from Drivethrurpg as being in post editing development. Huh?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. It's an &quot;Advance PDF&quot; which means they're still collecting errata on it. Says it on the DTRPG page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Note:</b> This is the Advance PDF version. We will be collecting errata comments for a few weeks before updating the PDF and preparing the Softcover version of the book. Anyone who purchases this Advance PDF will automatically get the final PDF added to their account on DriveThruRPG and receive a coupon for the Softcover version when it is ready. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T15:20:13-08:00","id":1362966,"title":"","content":"Ah ok. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T14:16:15-08:00","id":1363191,"title":"","content":"Is there a link for feedback? I'm idling away some downtime at work, and drivethru is blocked.<br /> <br /> The armors only list the soft values granted by tags, but all armor has 1 soft before tags increase it. Although, it might just be listing out the tag values, but I just wanted to provide the feedback to give someone a chance to verify.<br /> <br /> edit: Also to add for anyone perusing this thread that hasn't bought it, don't let this minor tidbit deter you, it's a really cool book. The characters are well written and generated otherwise. Just seems like a usability thing for pregen character sheets to have final values instead of just the tag values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 01-24-2020, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T16:56:16-08:00","id":1363531,"title":"","content":"That is the final value. You should never see armor that doesn\u2019t have at least Soft 1 as a tag. That\u2019s that 1 level of soft armor all armor has. You don\u2019t add +1 to the listed value of all armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T06:26:26-08:00","id":1363611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1363191#post1363191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a link for feedback? I'm idling away some downtime at work, and drivethru is blocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>The link should have been in the email when you purchased it, but try this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We're closing it soon, so please get it in this week if you can!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T10:07:51-08:00","id":1363650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1363531#post1363531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the final value. You should never see armor that doesn\u2019t have at least Soft 1 as a tag. That\u2019s that 1 level of soft armor all armor has. You don\u2019t add +1 to the listed value of all armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, page 126, &quot;All armor provides<br /> one point of Soft armor by default.&quot;<br /> <br /> and then the Soft Armor Tag-<br /> &quot;Soft armor increases the Difficulty of the Inflict<br /> Damage Stunt by 1.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, either the tag increases the Default of 1, or the first tag doesn't actually do anything. If you have the tag &quot;Soft 1&quot; you have a value of Soft 2. If you have &quot;Soft 2&quot;, you have a value of Soft 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1363611#post1363611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The link should have been in the email when you purchased it, but try this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forms.gle/4NvD6VL4WvY9URnT7 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We're closing it soon, so please get it in this week if you can!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha! That's what I get for not reading my emails. I just went straight to the link I was redirected to for download. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T21:43:48-08:00","id":1363734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1363650#post1363650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, page 126, &quot;All armor provides<br /> one point of Soft armor by default.&quot;<br /> <br /> and then the Soft Armor Tag-<br /> &quot;Soft armor increases the Difficulty of the Inflict<br /> Damage Stunt by 1.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, either the tag increases the Default of 1, or the first tag doesn't actually do anything. If you have the tag &quot;Soft 1&quot; you have a value of Soft 2. If you have &quot;Soft 2&quot;, you have a value of Soft 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>The soft tag doesn\u2019t say it increases your soft armor, it says what soft armor does. It\u2019s granting you the soft armor. It\u2019s not a coincidence that all the example armors in the core all have at least the soft 1 tag. They have it because page 126 says all armor has 1 soft armor. There\u2019s no hidden soft armor tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T14:13:44-08:00","id":1364031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1363734#post1363734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The soft tag doesn\u2019t say it increases your soft armor, it says what soft armor does. It\u2019s granting you the soft armor. It\u2019s not a coincidence that all the example armors in the core all have at least the soft 1 tag. They have it because page 126 says all armor has 1 soft armor. There\u2019s no hidden soft armor tag.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see that reading having credence, but it doesn't seem definitive to me. To me it seemed like the phrasing for Weapons, that-<br /> &quot;By default, all weapons give an Enhancement<br /> bonus of 1 and are close range only.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't have to buy a tag for the Enhancement, and provides a nice 1 to 1 counterpoint to the default Soft Armor.<br /> <br /> The one thing that gives me pause is that in \u00c6on Armor gets an extra 5 dots of tags, while weapons get 4, which could be accounting for having to always buy at least Soft Armor 1, but it could also just be that with wanting to make Complete 3, and put complete on everything, they just ran out of tags too quickly.<br /> <br /> I also recall this coming up before in the Ask a Devs thread, but it got blown away, so I might need to ask again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T14:46:27-08:00","id":1364037,"title":"","content":"Quality for weapons and soft armor for armor are worded diffidently. The quality tag talks about increasing the default enhancement while soft armor just says it increases the difficulty to buy the injury stunt. Soft armor isn\u2019t the general term for increases to the difficulty to buy the injury stunt, it\u2019s just a source of such a modification. The soft armor tag isn\u2019t increasing your soft armor.<br /> <br /> If you look at the weapon stats in the core you can see that everything has +1 enhancement even without the quality tag (Unfortunately one of the 2 examples of the quality tag either has the wrong quality tag or enhancement). Contrast that with the armor where every piece of armor has the soft tag. There isn\u2019t a single piece of armor that doesn\u2019t possess the soft tag. Even the most basic, least helpful piece of armor has soft 1. It doesn\u2019t make sense for it to be 1+soft 1 from a game design perspective. That effectively makes all armor a plus 2 difficulty to the injury stunt. They could have just started the difficulty at 1 and added to it, or made the base rule that all armor starts at soft armor 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T15:58:31-08:00","id":1364054,"title":"","content":"Every armor comes with a free instance of the Soft tag. This is included in the armor\u2019s stats - you don\u2019t look at the armor\u2019s Soft value and as one to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T17:10:12-08:00","id":1364070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1364037#post1364037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quality for weapons and soft armor for armor are worded diffidently. The quality tag talks about increasing the default enhancement while soft armor just says it increases the difficulty to buy the injury stunt. Soft armor isn\u2019t the general term for increases to the difficulty to buy the injury stunt, it\u2019s just a source of such a modification. The soft armor tag isn\u2019t increasing your soft armor.<br /> <br /> If you look at the weapon stats in the core you can see that everything has +1 enhancement even without the quality tag (Unfortunately one of the 2 examples of the quality tag either has the wrong quality tag or enhancement). Contrast that with the armor where every piece of armor has the soft tag. There isn\u2019t a single piece of armor that doesn\u2019t possess the soft tag. Even the most basic, least helpful piece of armor has soft 1. It doesn\u2019t make sense for it to be 1+soft 1 from a game design perspective. That effectively makes all armor a plus 2 difficulty to the injury stunt. They could have just started the difficulty at 1 and added to it, or made the base rule that all armor starts at soft armor 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I see both readings as plausible, as there is some ambiguity. I've encountered both readings in the wild, as it were.<br /> <br /> I'll take the pregens and conversation here as confirmation for the interpretation that you must spend 1 tag on Soft armor. Also makes some sense with Armor getting an extra tag over Weapons in \u00c6on for the same cost. <br /> <br /> Thanks all for the time and talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T17:37:54-08:00","id":1364073,"title":"","content":"Bunyip is one of the devs so if they say it\u2019s meant to be that way you can take that as how the rules intended, despite the ambiguity in the presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T17:57:33-08:00","id":1364074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1364073#post1364073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bunyip is one of the devs so if they say it\u2019s meant to be that way you can take that as how the rules intended, despite the ambiguity in the presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Bunyip and I chat over on the discord often. I know they developed the ready made characters and wrote for the other books.<br /> <br /> Thanks for looking out though.<br /> <br /> Edit: just to account for any ambiguity in my own text, this post was really just to confirm amicable resolution to the conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T21:06:47-08:00","id":1364096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1362697-tc-aeon-ready-made-characters-trinity-continuum-aeon?p=1364054#post1364054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every armor comes with a free instance of the Soft tag. This is included in the armor\u2019s stats - you don\u2019t look at the armor\u2019s Soft value and as one to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to clarify as I\u2019ve made an error above. All armor comes with one Soft armor tag, but it\u2019s not \u2018free\u2019, it does come out of the Wealth + tags limit. Apologies for that confusion. However, the rest is correct -you don\u2019t add one to the armor\u2019s listed Soft rating.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I should have said:<br /> <br /> Every armor comes with an instance of the Soft tag that counts against the number of positive tags you can take. This is included in the armor\u2019s stats - you don\u2019t look at the armor\u2019s Soft value and as one to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}